Road to 1.0: 61% — 78 of 127 acceptance points delivered (measured 2026-09-28)
6 of 23 catalogue items complete; all 15 gates open. Counts are editorial catalogue bullets, not a fixed-scope completion percentage or release acceptance. ACT-32/M3 and ACT-33/M4 remain in progress.
- M0 in-progress — Stabilize the campaign and close the current AI findings: Every retained campaign-safety scenario passes against the rules that ship, including the pending-assault regression that had been frozen at rules 17. The wider gates behind M0 are still open.
- M1 in-progress — Client states and unification victory: A contestable two-thirds Unification bid is playable, city-states seat beside the realms, and a realm may take another as its paid client whose hearths stand behind its bid. Client capture outcomes and transfers between patron and client remain.
- M2 in-progress — A complete magical discovery loop: Seams are hidden under Ashfall glass, found by a paid survey, drawn for ashglass and required before Arcane Theory; Unbinding answers a working with a working and costs its caster a round. Reactive interception and personal path growth remain.
- M3 in-progress — Empire delegation and coordinated orders: Rules/save 34 adds opt-in visible-threat reinforcement with bounded quiet-turn holds, preserving physical minimum guards and direct-order priority. Joined authored mature-realm controls, partial refusals and exact AI-inclusive saved continuation are verified. Patrol/escort roles, reusable army-order templates, broader governors and organic-scale acceptance remain. Separate verification scopes: implementation 2146, publication 2146, affected browser 49, built production 2, local/live Pages 35/35, compatibility 102. These overlapping counts are not additive. Source f33a816f3a853229695b902af007e4e3f3547275; publication abb2369fd289a549c59704fbbe4aa6fb8354bafb. Evidence: ~/Work/Theandril/docs/development/2026-09-27-reinforcement-logistics/
- M4 in-progress — Supply, trade and sustained military operations: Rules/save 34 adds paid source-specific foreign supply access through ordinary proposals and acceptance. Fees pay once on acceptance; imported land/harbor supply retains ordinary blockade, ownership, war and expiry constraints. Participant-only disclosures, AI fee reserves, save/replay and uncertain-payment recovery are verified. This grants no movement rights. Trade routes/interception, taxation, material supply costs and broader coordinated operations remain. Separate verification scopes: implementation 2146, publication 2146, affected browser 49, built production 2, local/live Pages 35/35, compatibility 102. These overlapping counts are not additive. Source f33a816f3a853229695b902af007e4e3f3547275; publication abb2369fd289a549c59704fbbe4aa6fb8354bafb. Evidence: ~/Work/Theandril/docs/development/2026-09-27-reinforcement-logistics/ Final rules 34 headline standard-map/12-realm/seed20260905 measurements: Standard 233 turns, 0 submitted refusals, 0 automatic blocked routes; Long 311 turns, 0 submitted refusals, 0 automatic blocked routes; Epic 349 turns, 0 submitted refusals, 0 automatic blocked routes. Matched frozen rules 33 headline results: Standard 233 turns; Long 311 turns; Epic 349 turns. The report contains eighteen runs: nine configurations, each under 33 and 34. Counters and seeds remain distinct. No target-band acceptance or price change is inferred. ACT-38 and DH-021 stay open.
- M5 in-progress — Independent powers, political pressure and agent roles: Twenty-four city-states are authored, playable and courtable as clients. Clans, pirates, mercenaries, enclaves and the political layer are not built.
- M6 open — Epochs, crises and the living campaign: Navigate eras, upheaval and world crises rather than a flat timeline.
- M7 open — Progression depth and the third victory path: Two victory paths exist; the third and the deeper progression behind it do not.
- M8 in-progress — Authored breadth, exploration and final presentation: Twenty-four cultures, seven map types and the city-state register are published; the quantitative content and art targets are not met.
- M9 open — Authoritative online campaigns: The deployed game is single-player; no server, rooms or reconnect exist.
- M10 open — Sustained proof and release signoff: Prove the integrated release at scale and across browsers, then sign the gates.

